  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">University Partnerships</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Haiti):  In the agriculture sector, innovation and evidence-based approaches that are adapted to local conditions are critical to increasing production and productivity, transforming goods, and creating and strengthening market linkages. Growing the base of specific skill sets helps address complex issues such as building human and institutional capacity and identifying areas of research for the benefit of local institutions and producers. The Agricultural University Partnership activity aims to support a network of Haitian institutions in developing an agricultural research agenda that is aligned with national development, food security, and resilience priorities. The goal is to create a center that will strengthen agricultural education, training, research, and outreach activities, and link farmers with the private sector. Using FY 2022 funding, this activity will increase institutional capacities and social capital to better meet the needs of the agricultural sector in Haiti, develop revenue-generating services at local institutions to ensure that farmers have continued access to services, and support research centers to showcase high-potential agricultural technologies and strategies to sustainably intensify smallholder production systems..The focus on local institutions aligns with the mission&apos;s integrated resilience-focused strategy and aims to have deeper engagements with local universities and research centers in Haiti, more specifically in the two mission-designated Resilience Focus Zones. Given the continued interest in agriculture professions and the capacity to conduct applied research, USAID plans to use FY 2022 funds to better connect academic institutions to the private sector, extension organizations, and farmers. This activity will contribute to addressing the challenges associated with variable cropping systems, low productivity, and support demand-driven applied research.... .</narrative>
  </description>
